{
 "$comment": "AEP-0002 Annex A machine-usable mapping fixture for the Hermes Agent table (the SHELL-hook generation). SOURCE PROVENANCE, stated: the vendor publishes no typed schema artifact — payload shapes were read from the repository at tag v2026.7.7.2 (design record: docs/components/adapter-hermes-design.md, file:line cited) and every payload carries telemetry_schema_version \"hermes.observer.v1\" in extra (pinned here as the drift sentinel; a different value is the re-verify trigger). Each entry pins the pure envelope->events mapping at the adapter default posture (capture metadata; attention.* redacted): input is one stdin envelope {hook_event_name, tool_name, tool_input, session_id, cwd, extra}; expected is an ARRAY of {type, data, subject?}. Envelope identity (session_id -> session; the REAL per-turn turn_id -> run, stamped by the daemon; tool_call_id pairing; approval pre/post pairing by session|pattern_key) is runtime state, pinned by the reference adapter smoke. OBSERVE-ONLY: the shim never blocks and never injects context. The vendor approval gate is observed read-only — since AEP-0008 its card carries the vendor decision menu as options data and declares respond_via [oob]; answers ride via oob. The clarify ask-the-user tool additionally maps a FORM OVERLAY (AEP-0006 kind form, one field, respond_via [oob]) beside its pinned tool events: the tool trio never moves, the pre card mirrors the vendor entry-point choice normalization, the post result classifies answered (a picked choice = its structural 1-based id; Other = redacted-gated free text) / timeout (the vendor return-contract sentinels) / dismissed (cancel, undeliverable, empty, blocked, error).",
 "identity": {
  "session_from": "session_id (the serializer falls back to parent_session_id on subagent hooks — delegation lands on the parent). APPROVAL EXCEPTION, source-pinned: the approval fire sites pass no session kwarg, so pre_approval_request / post_approval_response ALWAYS carry session_id \"\" — identity rides only as extra.session_key (CLI surface: equals the session id; gateway surface: a platform-scoped key). The adapter joins session_key against sessions it has already seen and otherwise degrades to the unknown lane (runtime state, pinned by the reference adapter smoke).",
  "run_from": "extra.turn_id (REAL per-turn id, verbatim — no synthesis; pre_llm_call opens, on_session_end closes per turn)",
  "$comment": "tool_call_id pairs the tool trio; the approval pre/post pair is keyed session|pattern_key in the daemon."
 },
